Great! Let's build a simple substring-match CLI application in Rust. This app will read a file, search for a given substring, and print the lines that contain the substring.

Here are the steps we'll follow:

1. Set up a new Rust project.
2. Read command-line arguments.
3. Read the file content.
4. Search for the substring in each line.
5. Print the matching lines.

### Step 1: Set up a New Rust Project

First, make sure you have Rust installed. If not, you can install it from [rust-lang.org](https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install).

Create a new Rust project:
```sh
